,title,link,text,language,family
0,Rangpuri language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rangpuri_language,"Rangpuri (Rangpuri: অংপুরি Ôṅgpuri or অমপুরি Ômpuri) is an eastern Indo-Aryan language of the Bengali-Assamese branch, spoken in Rangpur Division in Bangladesh, northern West Bengal and western Goalpara of Assam in India. [6]",Rangpuri,Indo-European
1,Indo-European languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo-European_languages,Written evidence of Indo-European appeared during the Bronze Age in the form of Mycenaean Greek and the Anatolian languages of Hittite and Luwian.,Rangpuri,Indo-European
2,"The Sound of Indo-European Music (Compilation) - YouTubeRangpuri language — GrokipediaIndo-European Music - playlist by kinoid | SpotifyRangpuri, Bangladesh - worldmission.mediaIndo-European Music (UPDATED) - YouTubeIndo-European languages - Wikipedia",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WgHSW774Q-4,"Sep 8, 2019 · In this video, I compiled music from all the major Indo-European languages. I hope you enjoy these great songs! Rangpuri, also known as Rajbanshi or Kamtapuri, maintains its strongest presence in the Rangpur Division of northwestern Bangladesh, where it serves as the primary vernacular for communities in rural and semi-urban areas. Indo-European Music · Playlist · 485 songs · 19 likes It has historical roots in the Rajbongshi kingdom and is predominantly spoken in the northern regions of Bangladesh and India, with approximately 15 million speakers. It’s also present in Nepal. Content consumption in Rangpuri-speaking areas is diverse, with a mix of traditional and modern media. Collection of Indo-European Music! Written evidence of Indo-European appeared during the Bronze Age in the form of Mycenaean Greek and the Anatolian languages of Hittite and Luwian.",Rangpuri,Indo-European
3,Rangpuri language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Rangpuri_language,"Rangpuri, also known as Rajbanshi or Kamtapuri, maintains its strongest presence in the Rangpur Division of northwestern Bangladesh, where it serves as the primary vernacular for communities in rural and semi-urban areas.",Rangpuri,Indo-European
4,Indo-European Music - playlist by kinoid | Spotify,https://open.spotify.com/playlist/7kgyQDDKh5svTahzdt5C7C,Indo-European Music · Playlist · 485 songs · 19 likes,Rangpuri,Indo-European
5,"Rangpuri, Bangladesh - worldmission.media",https://worldmission.media/languages-of-the-world/rangpuri,"It has historical roots in the Rajbongshi kingdom and is predominantly spoken in the northern regions of Bangladesh and India, with approximately 15 million speakers. It’s also present in Nepal. Content consumption in Rangpuri-speaking areas is diverse, with a mix of traditional and modern media.",Rangpuri,Indo-European
